  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In the heart of the hilltop village of Mougins, on Place du Commandant Lamy, La Place de Mougins is a fine-dining restaurant recognised by the Michelin Guide (selection, two place settings) and Gault&amp;Millau, run by chef Denis Fétisson. A signature menu is offered at €130.</p>

      <h2>Your dog at La Place</h2>
      <p>The restaurant lists on its own website, among its menus, "Nos amis les chiens" at €25. The Mougins tourist office listing (Regional Tourism Committee portal, updated 19 May 2026) gives the conditions: animals accepted "on a leash, next to their owners, small-sized dogs", with a dog menu at €25. A large dog should therefore be mentioned when booking. No distinction is made between dining room and terrace. Rated 9.7/10 on TheFork (over 1,200 reviews) and 4.7/5 on Tripadvisor, the place is in high demand.</p>

      <h2>Table, hours and capacity</h2>
      <p>La Place de Mougins is listed in the Michelin Guide and rated 15/20, "Table Remarquable", by Gault&amp;Millau. The restaurant is open Thursday to Monday, for lunch until 1:30pm and dinner until 9:30pm; it is closed on Tuesday and Wednesday (the website announces modified hours in August). According to the tourist office, the air-conditioned dining room seats 60 and the covered, shaded terrace 40. Menus on the website: "Le midi de la Place" at €48, "Origine" at €85, "Signature" at €130, vegan menu at €85, featured-ingredient menu at €145 or €180, children's menu at €30 according to the tourist office.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: this is a very popular fine-dining table (tight hours, closed Tuesday and Wednesday) — book ahead and mention your dog, who even gets their own €25 menu.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The village of Mougins, with its cobbled lanes and art galleries, is a pleasant stroll before or after the meal.</p>
